    "## 2. What does a row represent?\n",
    "\n",
    "Each row appears to represent one patient record: `PatientID` is unique in this file. There are no dates, follow-up visits, recruitment details or site identifiers, so this is treated as a cross-sectional table. Unique IDs alone do not prove that the records are independent or authentic clinical observations.\n",
    "\n",
    "`PatientID` is an identifier; `Diagnosis` is a recorded binary status used for sample description. Question 1 compares two memory indicators and their MMSE distributions; question 2 compares two functional measures; question 3 evaluates sensitivity to quality exclusions. Demographics and medical-history indicators provide groups; lifestyle, clinical and assessment fields provide measurements. `DoctorInCharge` is a constant confidentiality placeholder and cannot support comparisons between doctors.\n"
   ]
  },
